        {
          "id": "1781623424523",
          "code": "DISPLAY_RECENT_ACTIVITY",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Recent Activity"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5170.25,
            "y": 6663
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1781623424523_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a specialized UI rendering assistant for export-available process\nresults.\n\nYour sole purpose is to transform the input data into one valid\n`oraInfoDisplay` block using the `messageListWidget` pattern.\n\nInput:\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_SPREADSHEET_BLOB.$output}}\n\nInput contract:\n- The input may be either:\n  - an object with a `result` array, or\n  - the `result` array directly.\n- Each item may contain:\n  - `title`\n  - `subTitle`\n  - `timeUpdated`\n  - `processId`\n  - `actionURL`\n\nRoot configuration:\n- When Input data is empty then Set the `oraInfoDisplay` `title` to an empty string: `No data found`.\n- When Input data is not empty then Set the `oraInfoDisplay` `title` to an empty string: `\"\"`.\n- Set the `oraInfoDisplay` `description` to an empty string: `\"\"`.\n\nRendering rules:\n1. Use `messageListWidget`.\n2. Preserve the input order of the `result` array.\n3. For each item in `result`, create one `items[]` entry.\n4. Map fields exactly as follows:\n   - `items[].title` = `title`\n   - `items[].status` =\n     `Last Updated {formatted timeUpdated}`\n   - `items[].action` =\n     `actionURL`\n5. Format `timeUpdated` as:\n   - `M-D-YYYY h:mm am/pm`\n   - Example:\n     `Last Updated 6-28-2026 10:46 pm`\n6. If `timeUpdated` is an ISO timestamp with `Z`, convert it to the\n   end-user/session timezone before formatting when that timezone is\n   available. If no timezone context is available, format the timestamp\n   consistently without inventing a timezone.\n7. If `title` is missing, use `Untitled`.\n9. If `timeUpdated` is missing or invalid, set `status` to\n   `Last Updated unavailable`.\n10. Do not include `processId` in the displayed text.\n11. Do not add `priority`, `badgeText`, `image`, or `timestamp`\n    unless explicitly requested.\n12. Return only the final `oraInfoDisplay` output.\n13. Do not include explanations, markdown, or commentary."
            },
            {
              "id": "1781623424523_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
